  "content": {
    "title": "Champions League bracket 2026: Barcelona and Liverpool crash out, full schedule",
    "text": "Updated April 14, 2026, 5:46 p.m. ETThe last eight teams standing in the 2025-26 UEFA Champions League were narrowed down to six on Tuesday, with Paris Saint-Germain and Atletico Madrid securing their spots in the semifinals.PSG won 2-0 at Anfield behind two goals from Ousmane Dembele on Tuesday night to give the defending champions a 4-0 aggregate. Meanwhile, Barcelona stormed back from a two-goal deficit in the first half – only for Atletico to score and hold on for a 3-2 aggregate victory despite Barca's 2-1 win on the night.PSG will face Bayern Munich or Real Madrid in the semifinals, which begin on April 28, while Atletico will face Arsenal or Sporting Lisbon. The two other quarterfinal ties will be decided on Wednesday, April 15.Here's a look at the Champions League bracket entering play Tuesday: Champions League bracket QuarterfinalsTuesday, April 14Paris Saint-Germain 2, Liverpool 0 – PSG wins 4-0 on aggregateBarcelona 2, Atletico Madrid 1 – Atletico wins 3-2 on aggregateWednesday, April 153 p.m.: Bayern Munich vs. Real Madrid – Bayern leads 2-1 on aggregate3 p.m.: Arsenal vs. Sporting CP – Arsenal leads 1-0 on aggregate Semifinals scheduleApril 28/29 and May 5/6PSG vs. Real Madrid/Bayern MunichAtletico Madrid vs. Arsenal/Sporting CP Champions League results todayParis Saint-Germain 2, Liverpool 0 – PSG wins 4-0 on aggregateBarcelona 2, Atletico Madrid 1 – Atletico wins 3-2 on aggregate When is Champions League final?The 2026 Champions League final is set for May 30 at the Puskas Arena in Budapest, featuring a matchup of the two semifinal winners.The USA TODAY app gets you to the heart of the news — fast.Download for award-winning coverage, crosswords, audio storytelling, the eNewspaper and more.",
